BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Guarini Walk Around Occom Pond
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260903T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260903T130000
DTSTAMP:20260814T105131Z
UID:guarini-48871@free-food-dartmouth
SEQUENCE:0
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:Original event page(s):\nhttps://guarinigrad.dartmouth.edu/eve
 nts/2026/09/03/guarini-walk-around-occom-pond-7/\nhttps://apply.gs.dartmou
 th.edu/register/?id=151c45a6-6aab-4b79-8b8d-218df28d09c2\nhttps://guarinig
 rad.dartmouth.edu\n\nDescription:\nWalk Around Occom Pond\nJoin the Associ
 ate Dean of Guarini Graduate Student Affairs for a reflective walk around 
 Occom Pond\, followed by a coffee or tea break at Ramekin. This event offe
 rs a chance to connect with fellow graduate students\, postdocs and facult
 y in a relaxed\, natural setting\, promoting well-being and community spir
 it. Invite your faculty advisor or faculty mentor and you can both receive
  a $6 coupon for Ramekin and a Guarini Mug will be provided to participant
 s (limited to one each).\nMeet in front of the Guarini School\, Anonymous 
 Hall – across from Ramekin Cafe.\nGuariniGrad Dialogues\nare a series of
  events designed to bring graduate students\, postdocs\, and faculty toget
 her in informal settings to foster empathy\, understanding\, and a deeper 
 sense of community. By creating spaces where differing views\, perspective
 s\, and circumstances can be shared and appreciated\, these dialogues aim 
 to strengthen connections within the Dartmouth community and foster a sens
 e of belonging.\n*Guarini graduate students include all PhD\, MA\, MALS\, 
 MET\, and MFA students\; and MS students in Engineering\, Computer Science
 \, and Earth Sciences.\n\nSponsor / organizer: GuariniGRAD\n\nAudience: Gu
 arini graduate students and postdocs\n\nSource: Guarini\n\nWhy this was in
 cluded: food keyword near service context in summary\n\nFood availability 
 is inferred from the source listing\; verify details before attending.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260814T105131Z
LOCATION:Anonymous Hall
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://guarinigrad.dartmouth.edu/events/2026/09/03/guarini-walk-aroun
 d-occom-pond-7/
X-MICROSOFT-CDO-BUSYSTATUS:FREE
END:VEVENT
